can say need them to (1) give the beat/footage list; (2) confirm facts with screenshot; then we can finalize.\n\nGiven we are already in PRE mode because no manifest, full package outputs are \"草案\"; there is no proper release. So it should not be \"READY\".\n\nCould status be NEEDS_DECISION: need user to provide content beat list and POA-level access. Yes.\n\nLet's revisit mode under equivalent input. Let's formalize PRE explanation:\n- Evidence available: content unit \"出锅过程\" claims only one asset; even if we count that as unit descriptor, no demonstration that a relevant beat for *promise elements* can be traced (e.g., beer lees base, the local meat) or matches each \"coverage declared is '有' or found absent\". No beat list, no support matrix. So no legal equivalent evidence.\n- It is not MIXED or FINAL because second-level (manifest available) not reached. This is first-level PRE.\n- Even if you said: \"we've shot it\" - filming a video isn't a manifest. This is exactly \"拍了42分钟\" style.\n- state: all PUBLISHING outputs are 草案; realized_payoff cannot be claimed. upper = content_promise (用户 intent: 勾食欲 + 老手艺 + 到店/办卡, but note latter under goal states UNKNOWN; non-promise list: 祖传 no, 秘方? Actually user says \"不能说什么祖传秘方\" -&gt; not claim).\n- In content_promise, we can infer intent: display old craft authenticity and this is distinct from typical casually stir-fried? The user did not spell \"content promise\" but they did define: \"想让观众知道这道菜真的是老手艺，不是随便炒的\" — treat it as planned promise, expressed; not as \"we promise clients\". Upper based on it. Fines: actual footage quality is unknown, so copy claim to be cautious.\n\nNow define output details:\n\nmaster_package:\n- cover description: 画面：取「收汁/出锅」油亮汁滚的瞬间近景（frame should be in upper area free of 底300px遮挡）。文字层级:\n  line1: 「这锅收了十二年的红烧肉」?? Wait: 文字 would claim \"十二年\". Make confident? It's user-claimed. Use draft and stated confirmation. Let's make cover as: 第一行大字 「红烧肉 · 收汁出锅」 + 第二行小字「自家黄酒糟卤打底」. Then title can hold a stronger claim. Actually Big text must not be duplication. Title (conceptual) e.g. \"我劝你先备好饭\"?? claims wanting. Hmm.\nFirst idea: Because an accidental thing: \"多备一碗饭\" creates a slight call to action appetitive rather than business? It's okay.\n\nLet's systematically design titles as competitors:\n- SITUATION candidate: 「一锅红烧肉出锅前的最后40秒」→ shows scene, gap: what's in it; but with enough sizzle if vid. It is more like 描述 a period. But if listed, equivalent \"看见锅里发生的事\". Might be weak as headline.\n- QUOTABLE_LINE candidate: needs speech; not allowed no quote invent? We don't have any owner voice/quote. Actually QUOTABLE_LINE could be a phrase without quotes (金句): \"老手艺从来不用喊\" (meaning twelve-year craft doesn't need shout), but that is a maxim and title says \"你会看到一句话\" — we could see words at the end. Good and expresses craft+without bragging \"call it old craft loudly\" perhaps good.\n- INFORMATION candidate: 「上海红烧肉糖色之外，还有一勺黄酒糟卤」 — the info fact about own pickled黄酒糟卤 as a base. But if actual video doesn't show: need pre-register and probably add specific overlay. Draft okay. \n- CONTRADICTION candidate: 「做了十二年的红烧肉，靠的不是秘方」 — directly bypass \"祖传秘方\": due to user explicit non-promise, this title mocks \"秘方\"? Contrapositive trick but it warns about \"秘方\" - Might reintroduce? Non-promise: say no ancestral secret recipe; so title \"不是秘方\" can create a negative suggestion, probably okay but captures attention: \"祖传秘方\" typed? Danger that searchable content includes '秘方' → irrelevant. It works with real data points \"十二年\". Actually note title includes \"十二年\" (truthful user self-report).\n\nWait: \"十二年\" is a long duration in this lane; great.\nCheck \"不要随便炒的\" support in footage: Can't know.\n\n- IDENTITY: perhaps not.\n\nChoose recommended: `SITUATION`: 「红烧肉收汁那几秒，最熬人」 =&gt; food \"sauces down\"? Sweet sounds like \"等饭\" etc. Reference \"preparing a rice bowl before serving\"? Let's leave visual scene:\nRecommended SITUATION route A: \"看这锅红烧肉收汁，我默默去热了碗米饭\".\nHmm \"我\" is inventory? since a cooking video watched first person.\n\nLet me choose title as an INFORMATION because it differentiates (data claims in user content):\n「我家红烧肉卖了十二年，底气是一勺自家腌的黄酒糟卤」\nBut face repeated in other lines? Wait, it's too length maybe 27+ characters; Douyin recommendation ≤15字 by platform table. Many Douyin titles longer than 15 chars? The \"建议长度\" ≤15字. So make concise: \"红烧肉不香？那是少了这勺黄酒糟卤\" (20 chars, still long) hmm. Since caption splits. Okay, but title-like. Another popular title \"这锅肉，是等你下饭的\" etc. Let's not focus.\nDouyin as feed-only, what matters first 3 seconds. Title isn't displayed dominant (under video, maybe visible). Title length ≤15 suggested but not a strict platform hard gate, though it's a rule we shouldn't violate. Use short 10-12.\n\nMy proposed candidates (draft set) in full:\n1. SITUATION: 「红烧肉出锅，先盛一碗饭」 (~12) \n2. INFORMATION: 「这锅肉香，是黄酒糟卤给的」 (that's 14)\n3. QUOTABLE_LINE: 「手艺老不老，锅里看得出」 (~11) — Good, implies claim \"in the pot you can see whether craft is real\", fits. But it's an assertion; may promise \"看起来\"? okay.\n4. CONTRADICTION: 「香了十二年的红烧肉，不靠秘方」 (17)\nRecommended: (2) perhaps because exact differentiation and resonates (even if you didn't see a jar on video; can be covered by caption/comment; but verify at preview).\nAnd honestly because user wants \"饮食知是老手艺而非随便炒\" and \"勾食欲\" both are in one: container? These titles satisfy.\nBut from a strict factual ledger, \"黄酒糟卤\" \"十二年\" are from user's own info; we haven't had it verified; mark route as drafts; if We mark F IDs absence, we might place their final use as pending confirmation.\n\nWait, do we need an actual ID for title facts to capture? In artifacts used_fact_refs[] maybe use pseudo: no id, we will write `fact_id: (en: user-report; 待登记)`? That is bad machine type. Instead use we keep out exact factual claims in recommended titles: Quotable line is safe \"店开了十二年\" vs. may not need store. We try no factual claims requiring ledger in titles? But if recommended titles no 12yr/糟卤, they lose the craft info; later second line on cover might use: \"十二年的本帮味\" (claims user report).\nIn Deliverable, we can on front stage present these candidates with labels saying the claims to be reconfirmed before posting. The ledger zero entries.\n\nNow what is the primary \"specific promises\": if we include factual references in publish copy, we can say \"需用户确认后登记\". But if we include full text final, we're acting like it can be published, not PRE. We can put in DELIVERY under \"推荐草稿\".\n\nThe final deliverable, as needed to an end user, must not show ledger-like conditions stated as \"未核实\"? But conditions such as \"发布前核对：\" in natural wording not forbidden? They prohibit the words \"unverified not to use\". They say \"禁止出现: '未核实，不得使用'这类便条' and '已删除等'\" in user delivery; because if you must not include something, remove it. Yet you must include user decisions required. The difference: we are not saying a sentence was added then removed; instead we note as a working state: \"发布前需要补充素材清单\" - normal user-oriented.\n\nTherefore we should not include claims like “十二年” in *final* user-facing if claims require evidence... Hmm—Actually the user (owner) is right there. He asserted it. He doesn't require self-certification. We are allowed to trust a client statement? Source = client statement for factual; however the discipline says verify source at output, source is \"用户自述（客户业务的事实主张）\"; that’s valid. Yes, source can own customer authorized; the only reason no registry is that our skill input didn't provide IDs. But we could in ASSUMPTIONS state it, and in full results still write facts with claims assumption= self-reported data and need subsequent registry if independent up-stream needs. Then release remains hold due to lack of coverage not due to fact. For user, we can directly produce titles and copy because all facts are from client's report. Formal fact ledger final: For each fact use the ID \"SELF-DECLARED-...\"? Again machine: matches not from registry -&gt; parse failure.\n\nA catch: The F4 ledger gate handles \"fact claims needing registration\". If no fact_refs exist, register NONE and that \"no independent fact claims are formally reflected in final delivery\". But we earlier include \"final\" publish copy with factual assertions - so not coherent. We can not treat user-stated facts as final assertions in this channel; we will frame those sentences as \"如果你确认这些句子，可以选用以下两行\" - suggestions, not final factual statements.\n\nLet's decide number of packaging routes:\nTrue same? There is one prominent tradeoff: 用哪一种为钩子 (appetite visual vs shop craft). Different failure situations: if appetizing, fails if audience doesn't click because in many result-first; if crafts, fails because audience doesn't care whether old; Add actual two routes. There is signal in industry-conditions: video is only to hook appetite; shop craft also user requested; could Be a two-lane media mix: different content to answer two different reasons.\n\n- Route A: 食欲钩子（视觉为主）: Title/caption frames of craving; failure when static looking. Good for Douyin first 3 seconds.\n- Route B: 信物钩子（\"真老店\"）: Evidence \"12 years\", \"Home-pickled wine lees\", \"no one else? etc.\"; Works for value and location? Fail when not being believed absent visual. But risk: it may not act as appetizer.\n\nHowever they could not share route: We must select and on behalf of the user (consider goal of store visits/card) Which? User wanted both. Recommend Route A as entry (to get views) and craft markers as second-level (captions/comment); but route is actual single? I'd rather say: the practical difference between putting \"appetite\" or \"old craft\" as main hook is a real option; describe each and when it would flop. Recommendation: Route A with craft footnotes because actual 40s footage is finished process, which will feed appetite best. So packaging_routes[]=2 routes. Verified.\n\nMaster package content:\n1 cover: On Douyin Douyin no matter about first in feed — first still = process close-up with good branch top safe 150? For safer:\n- select first_frame: pork close-up, gravy rolling (if present) during 收汁/颠勺/出锅? \"锅中汁水翻涌/蒸汽冒起的一瞬, by aligning camera mid.\" + relationship to cover: complementary (the cover for profile grid: a frame after the meat loaded in plate + visible texture + maybe chopsticks? all self). To note: \"无他人出镜：只拍锅、肉、手不过分? \"User says no one appears; hands? hand may appear. \"没有别人出镜\" doesn't mean no worker hands. But owner might be behind. Let cover choose \"第一帧\" from process itself, but keep not at dark intro.\n- On cover text, rule: no text over the meat, clean top/bottom lines inside safe:\nline 1 (main): 「收汁的红烧肉」\nline 2 (small): 「本帮·小馆」? Should be a \"who is it for/condition\" (谁能吃/条件): e.g. \"不怕胖的来\" no.\nline 2: \"老城区/黄酒糟卤底味\"? Wait line2 is 限定条件 (谁看、什么场合), small. We can write 小字「饿了再看」/「配饭警告」. Less relevant.\nMaybe: main \"红烧肉出锅\"; small \"自家黄酒糟卤\". Main title isn't same as final? Distinction: Visual takes \"白气\" to make move.\nGiven hyt: actual visuals unknown, output robust to making generic: \"first frame must show a shiny top, glossing movement, steam; If the clip starts with something else (potentially no meat) — a pre-roll/caption insert must pull frame.\" But suggesting remove if absent. To avoid PP-2 repetition, cover is used only on profile. content text: 3-6 characters: \"红烧肉\" - just.\nBut if user asked not forcing story: etc.\n\n2. title candidates:\nRoute A:\nA1/SITUATION: 「这锅肉收汁的样子，配得上三碗饭」\nBreak text not too long? 17, less. But Douyin advises ≤15 characters; can count: perhaps 16. Let's take 14 \"收汁那几秒，看得我想添饭\"; A bit generic.\n“闻到红烧肉收汁的味儿了。” (13) SITUATION.\nA2/INFORMATION: “底味是自己腌的黄酒糟卤” - say reason not carried by first? Actually 13.\nA3/QUOTABLE_LINE: 「老巷子里的红烧肉，是等出来的」 maybe.\nRoute B informational:\nB? 12-year old title:\n- “在这条巷子卖了十二年的红烧肉” 15 \n- “不是秘方，是肯花十二年” maybe, but this is a claim/creative line that contradicts (and non-promise supportive).\nrecommend A if we don't actually know the shot includes pouring lees.\n\nTitle final recommendation? If we lead with \"一勺黄酒糟卤\" and the image is only meat, first line still forces \"make sure to overlay caption near meat\": risk. Situation title less factual but actual smell/color can be created. Since mode PRE, list candidates label 待素材核实.\n\n4. publish_copy: Full text, start three lines separate: I compose (but not duplicate script e.g. no yammer):\n- Opening: to trigger an instant hunger/commitment:\n  “大半夜刷到这一条，别怪我没提醒你。”\n  “后厨这锅红烧肉，刚收到汁。”\n  “肉在锅里抖的那几下，比什么摆盘都强。”\n- Middle: only when the user confirms there is a caption that that's not in footage? Hmm.\n  “开店十二年, most of it is just everyday.”.\nActually the phrase perhaps should start with CTA: “明天中午有座吗？先看……” Wait CTA low risk doesn't ask store.\n- Closing issue concrete question one sentence answer: \"你吃红烧肉，是瘦肉派还是肥肉派？\" It's answerable and asks interaction.\n- Add \"片子里没说的是……\" is not allowed if no fact registry. But we have a fact not in the clip: user only filmed finished process; about the \"自家腌黄酒…\" is not a fact about method, can we do this only if fact_refs contains a corresponding record with ID. Currently impossible. So skip that structure. Instead comments/P.P. could fill missing.\nNo obvious CTA, comment design can add \"这条不是菜谱，就是给你看个馋\". It suggests maybe saving for? good.\n\n5. caption_rules:\n- 抖音 no sound? actual 现场声 probably lost. Food video needs juicy sizzle (加油气): if original sound is noisy/unusable, replace? Don't rely on unrealistic? In such background and proper recording, use high-quality close-mic sizzling instead of music maybe. For effect, need subtitles every phrases (but no lines?).\nActually content is live, probably only 40s with steam flame and sizzle; no talking; captions might be 3 informational lines. Suggest: add little on-screen text: \"收汁收到这个程度\" -&gt; enough; and end card? First one with title.\n- 单屏 word count: max unknown, in Douyin. Qualitative rule: one idea per screen, first screen (title card) fully legible, breaks by breath; avoid full-width bottom 300px region. Auto captions off.\n\nPlace texts at top 1/3 or upper area and + not cover dish; with high-contrast silhouette (warm/black).\n6. sound placement: Appetite layers:\n- Base: kitchen burners, sizzle + bubbles; no background music? recommended: keep natural sound + no crowd; overlay low rumble for braised pork? safe; Cue: pot noise at start, volume lift when gravy boils, gentle boil sounds are loud to light on a sizzle in the first two seconds if used. Intro effect? (short).\n- In a 40-45 second close-up, in the later part maybe fade and add a \"碗's chopsticks picking an angle?\" Not known.\n- no voice/narrator unless user can't produce. Simple.\n\n7. comment_design:\n- self first comment question, can be asked: “收汁收到什么程度算正好？我这个程度你们觉得过没过？” — This is good because any dish: \"这种程度会太干/刚好?\" ; asks viewer judgement which generates comment.\n- pre-embedded Q&amp;A group:\n  1. \"黄酒糟卤是啥？\" answer (new info beyond video): \"自己家腌的：黄酒+酒糟按比例放到一定时间，滤出来卤肉用；带着酒的香气去腻。具体做法教不了，但可以告诉你是自家腌的。——\" Wait this is expanding claims with method not provided in fact set, internal would need fact backing. Hmm. In comment answers new info should come from facts: short phrase: \"自腌的黄酒糟，带一丝酒香，是这锅肉的底味；肉是本地菜场当天买的，不是冻货。\" Good and grounded.\n  2. \"和别家比凭什么是美团第一\" -&gt; Probably a loaded claim best cautious: answer \"在这条街的本帮菜里，这两年美团销量排第一，不是全面第一；美团App上你自己能看到。\" Requires screenshot claimed; Actually this is factual (might be challenged) and \"你自己能看到\" prompts business. CTA doesn't...Answer an enquiry isn't CTA. Not strong, skip if uncertain.\n  3. \"多少钱 / 怎么点\" is potential business info. Answer could include \"店里菜单…\" But CTA low-risk doesn't allow; better handle via account's listed store? The rule: no any purchase/delivery/directives. A user after a good video posts address is naturally expected? If they ask \"店在哪\", telling address is an answer; it creates actual attraction. Is it prohibited? The no-CTA scenario: comments cannot include \"到店、预约\" etc. Under low risk interactions still no business actions. If someone asks location, I might respond \"可以在主页的店铺定位看到\" — that's guiding to a store visit/intentional path. Hard for low-risk. Option: Only \"on the profile store page when set up\" still yes commerce. Avoid pre-building it. If viewer asks, owner may answer as he chooses as part of a separate business authoring setting. In comment_design there may be no preplanned address.\n- \"我答不出\" prepared in case of live consumption: “有没有外卖?” Actually 属于 business; don't answer? Wait there's delivery and美团 sale relationship. The appropriate honest \"I cannot answer for now\" may apply not as \"不能回答\" but \"美团/堂食?\" Not needed.\nCould prepare an honest \"does it freeze?\" If they ask the recipe details: \"腌糟的配比是店里的，没法给；肉是哪个摊位买的可以说...\" Etc — actually some of it is trade secret? User says not to call a secret recipe; we don't deny.\n8. hashtags: Douyin topic pages (话题页引流) work. tags e.g. #本帮菜 #红烧肉 #老城区美食 #上海美食 #家常菜 #私房菜 ...? Need write each purpose; do not assert \"current hottest\". They're functional. Provide 4-5; set of 3? Need 3–8: we can give:\n   - #红烧肉: defines dish category, triggers algorithm classification for hungry users.\n   - #本帮菜: 菜系分类.\n   - #老城区美食 / #街坊小店: region/atmosphere user marker.\n   - #上海美食 (?) - user says 老城区, no city given! Must not assume city; statement says \"本帮红烧肉\" could be Shanghai. The user said 老城区巷子 and Douyin; do not invent location context city. #本帮菜 signals location; #本地生活 / #小馆子. If we don't know the city, omit city hashtag. Fine.\n   Rule: hashtags are \"平台机制\" not \"current hot\", e.g., category signals.\n9. on release checks:\n   * ① mute view: likely not understandable - a 45sec pans can see pot &amp; meat; if what happens is unclear, then need clear supertext... Since you need caption anyway.\n   * ② 1-second still: If strong first frame: only clicking, no caption for first 3s - \"肉汁在锅里冒泡\" clearly shows.\n   * ③ cover+title: yes in click.\n   * ④ save? Reason: \"自己想做？No: If a meat dish video, users don't want to make it — maybe \"带去吃的店\"? this implies desire to order the store, save as \"想吃/去\": possibly because the video is not a recipe, a pinned point is \"with friend go\" maybe. However according to Douyin feed-only, a \"save\" save semantics within Douyin = not typical. Release fifth important. We can say \"not likely saved (most viewing; converts to profile?); acceptable and then rely on that.\"\n   * ⑤ forward imagine: with a 'appetizing': to whom and what would they say? \"晚饭去哪?这家?\" = transport of desire... In delivery it is not CTA but natural. But for WeChat Channels, author share line Mandatory: it includes only with optional? recommended.\n   Provide a sharing line: need to deliver natural outcome: \"看饿了别找我，找这家\"?? Not location given. Let's craft empty-ish \"我把这家红烧肉最后收汁那 40 秒截下来了\" Hmm.\nBetter recommend share sentence: 「看饿了不许怪我——红烧肉出锅前的40秒」 natural.\n\nBut for WeChat user only says Douyin. We are only Douyin platform (platform_locked=Douyin); Douyin currently on table row? It lacks social spread route; author share optional; but still optional choose mark none? Wait in output author_share; only required where entrance includes social forwarding (WeChat channels). For Douyin not social lead. But can still written? yes \"optional\". Could include but not needed in adaptations.\n\nAdditional Douyin platform changes per rules:\n- Douyin=feed based; first three seconds are king, not captions title, so cut 40s: decide 3 second intro must have gravy sizzle — freeze on close-up; if opening black/pan, cut it.\n- cover on profile = choose most vivid frame but use crop; keep 3:4? DO NOT text at bottom third.\n- feed video caption length constraints from embedded ✓: reference \"Title suggestion ≤15字\"; ensure.\n- details: subtitles unlimited but qualitative; No one should be overlaid bottom 300.\n- vertical video full screen 1080×1920; if content was shot horizontal? Not known.\n- we prefer loops: \"make first frame after final frame\" so it feels looped (so repeat views) no hard cut at end.\nThis option: final frame can freeze/loop smoothly into start frame: gastronomy triggers repeated views.\n- For food content, actual \"spring\" and sound should be in first two seconds in Douyin.\n\nHowever we must not produce CS-level instruction \"cut etc\"? So in packaging stage, placement of intro cut isn't rewriting story; It's packaging placement? Editing/modify could be beyond strictly packaging? Generic PP output masters includes first frame and sound placement with cues and other finishing styles; cutting a frame within the captured action can stay \"镜头内选段\". but we avoid rewriting script. user does the actual cut action. \n\nHashtags and topics in v1.4:\n- hashtag list can include #本帮红烧肉 #红烧肉 #老城区美食 #小馆子 #下饭菜 #上海本帮菜? Wait, no city. Since unknown - but \"本帮\" is region-specific enough; choose.\nIn user docs: \"定位与话题用到具体城市后再补\" maybe.\n\nDelivery status = NEEDS_DECISION, but still present with tools:\nUser-decision demanded minimal: \n- \"这条素材里实际拍到哪些画面\" (because must know coverage; ask them to tick beat checklist e.g.; list all possible expected beats: 1) 收汁/咕嘟 2) 出锅装盘 3) 泼汁 4) 酒糟卤坛子 5) 筷子夹起拉丝/润等 — They should mark all that were really shot)\n- decide \"主要卖点: 食欲(视觉) vs 老店信服(信息)\".\nAnd if they want real store/card flow: separate business goal on active. In final decision wording level should not use \"CTA\"; talk naturally: words like \"本包按只引导关注评论收藏的配置。\"\n\nInteraction with user account: need ask? no forced.\n\nWe need state user's wish \"办储值卡\" mismatch: tell user:\n\"你提到希望看完能到店尝、最好还能顺手办张储值卡。这次的发布配置只到'关注/评论/收藏'。也就是说，视频里/文案里不会出现'来店办卡/储值'这类引导——你真要放这两步，得把经营目标（到店/办卡）和承接路径（定位、店员话术、卡规则）正式给出来，确认后我才能把文案改成那个方向。不硬推卡这条，说明里也替你守住了。\"\n\nWait—can the summary expose plan \"we won't\". yes.\n\nNow, user delivery claims should avoid numeric facts that need ledger? Will craft certain lines from the user data, but mark \"以下两句话由你口述的信息写成; before posting confirm on screen\" without negating. Facts can be included as part of editing because statements \"自家腌的黄酒糟卤打底、卖了十二年\" are in user original. If future \"F ledger: None\" then actual including them could be considered but we can explicitly say this run has no upstream fact list, treat as every fact in the output as \"店方自述\" awaiting user's confirmation— a potential \"Wait confirm\" rather than \"unverified delete\"; rules allow user-needed validation list.\n\nWait instruction prohibits words like \"未核实不可用\" from USER DELIVERY because it wants no unreliable sentences. To avoid suspicion, no final facts at all? Hmm. I'd struggle to make appetising Douyin caption without \"十二年/黄酒糟卤\".\n\nDo we need a nuanced way to satisfy rules:\n- All deliverable phrasing (visual words) derives from the content clip; no factual claims source from user data to check.\n- Use phrases like this:\n    title SITUATION: \"看完收汁那40秒，我默默去添了碗饭\" (no claim).\n    second line \"小馆子/做了十几年\" could be also factual. User: the source = owner.\nBut we never assert in names in metadata etc.\n\nIn the interest of realistic helpfulness over automated, I should include title candidates with them because end user wanted. Since actual owner is supplying facts as authoritative, making the pack un-usable is also failing. But we must not fabricate ID. The same for cover text '十二年的本帮红烧肉' - actual truth. On condition that before release the user confirms them (but they already did in narration; still need manifest checks plus fact registry not formalized) — status will be NEEDS_DECISION anyway.\n\nFACT_LEDGER should probably NOT be NONE solely due to no registry, because the text above has many factual statements. In that light, maybe think the logic says \"cannot claim this is the same thing as fact_refs\" – an outstanding omission. F4 asks to explicitly mark NONE only if no factual statements need to register; in our case not true. So NONE maybe contradicts. Perhaps you can list entries and use an explicit ID acknowledging source via reference \"user-input,未注册\", though valid